%I A400405 #8 Oct 01 2026 21:11:08
%S A400405 0,1,1,2,1,-1,-2,-3,-5,-2,-7,-9,-2,7,9,2,-7,-5,2,-3,-5,-2,-7,-9,-16,
%T A400405 -7,9,2,-7,-5,-12,-17,-5,-22,-27,-49,-22,27,49,22,-27,-49,-22,-71,-49,
%U A400405 22,-27,-49,-22,27,5,32,27,59,32,-27,-59,-86,-27,-113,-86,-199
%N A400405 Deterministic version of the random Fibonacci sequence, with signs from A076478 and the seed as (0,1).
%C A400405 Viswanath's random Fibonacci sequence flips a fair coin for each sign. Reading the signs off one fixed word instead gives a single integer sequence, and A076478 is normal in base 2, so every finite sign pattern still occurs with the frequency a coin would give it. Digit A076478(n-2) drives step n, with "1" adding and "0" subtracting.
%H A400405 Jwalin Bhatt, <a href="/A400405/b400405.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A400405 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/RandomFibonacciSequence.html">Random Fibonacci Sequence</a>
%H A400405 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Random_Fibonacci_sequence">Random Fibonacci sequence</a>
%F A400405 For n>=2: a(n) = a(n-1) + a(n-2) if A076478(n-2) = 1, otherwise a(n-1) - a(n-2).
%F A400405 Conjecture: lim_{n->oo} |a(n)|^(1/n) = 1.1319882487943... (A078416), Viswanath's constant.
%e A400405 A076478 begins 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, ..., so the signs applied at steps n = 2, 3, 4, ... are -, +, -, -, -, +, +, -, +, +, -, ...
%e A400405 a(2) = a(1) - a(0) = 1 - 0 = 1, since A076478(0) = 0.
%e A400405 a(3) = a(2) + a(1) = 1 + 1 = 2, since A076478(1) = 1.
%e A400405 a(4) = a(3) - a(2) = 2 - 1 = 1, since A076478(2) = 0.
%e A400405 a(5) = a(4) - a(3) = 1 - 2 = -1, since A076478(3) = 0.
%t A400405 Module[{c = Flatten[Array[Rest@IntegerDigits[# + 1, 2] &, 30]], a}, a[n_] := a[n] = If[n <= 1, n, a[n-1] + (2*c[[n-1]] - 1)*a[n-2]]; Array[a, 62, 0]]
%o A400405 (Python)
%o A400405 from itertools import count, islice, product
%o A400405 def A076478():  return (b for k in count(1) for v in product((0, 1), repeat=k) for b in v)
%o A400405 def A400405(n_terms):
%o A400405     a, d = [0, 1], list(islice(A076478(), n_terms))
%o A400405     for n in range(2, n_terms):
%o A400405         a.append(a[n-1] + a[n-2] if d[n-2] else a[n-1] - a[n-2])
%o A400405     return a
%o A400405 print(A400405(62))
%Y A400405 Cf. A000045, A076478, A078416, A399952.
%K A400405 sign,new
%O A400405 0,4
